# Breeze Skill Routing

When the user asks about Breeze capabilities or wants to perform a Breeze task, route to the correct skill:

| User wants to... | Skill |
|---|---|
| First-time setup, init, bootstrap | `/breeze:project setup` |
| Show / list / switch / create project, re-auth | `/breeze:project [show \| list \| use <name> \| create <name> \| auth \| status]` |
| Search features, code, "how does X work" | `/breeze:search` |
| Impact analysis, blast radius, "what breaks if X" | `/breeze:impact-analysis` |

## Recommended Pipeline

1. `/breeze:project setup` — link the repo to a Breeze project
2. `/breeze:search` — explore the functional, design, code and architecture graphs
3. `/breeze:impact-analysis` — cross-layer blast radius for a proposed change

## Project targeting

Every project-bound skill accepts a one-shot `--project <name|uuid>` override (or
a bare UUID / natural-language project hint) that applies to that invocation only
and does not touch `.breeze.json`. Persistent switches go through
`/breeze:project use <name|uuid>`. Full rules live in `CLAUDE.md` at the plugin
root.
